{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate. I did not request implementation source; the supplied tests were enough to map each obligation.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`**\n1. The harness combines every applicable contribution from the requirements that apply to the subject and its inputs.\n2. It deduplicates identical selections.\n3. It reports unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference.\n4. The complete set is supplied in the initial model request.\n5. A mandatory file must be visible under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`, meaning it follows `.gitignore`, untracked files are available, and files outside the project are excluded.\n6. A denied selection aborts under `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`. That requirement is cited, so I checked only that the case is exercised here.\n7. The clause that contributing requirements must cite this requirement and define their sources describes requirement text. It is not testable behaviour.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Combining contributions.**\n  - `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors]` checks the subject declaration, cited requirements, example declarations, term definitions and `{test}` items. It also checks that a distant requirement, an unrelated `impl` item and earlier evidence inputs are excluded.\n  - `fn[only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs]` checks which reference edges contribute.\n  - `fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` and `fn[test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node]` check anchor contributions. The first asserts the exact input list. The second asserts that only the selected node reaches the prompt.\n  - `fn[references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes]` and `fn[generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default]` cover reference-owning nodes and the discovery exclusions.\n  - `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` covers the site-review set, including cited requirements and terms.\n  - `book_commentary_reviews_supply_the_whole_passage_and_check_concordance` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` covers the book-commentary set, including cited requirements and terms.\n- **Deduplication.**\n  - `fn[citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once]` asserts that duplicate cites, a shared term and a repeated built-in each appear exactly once, with a total of 5 inputs.\n  - The bundle test shows the term cited from several places is counted once (2 definitions in total).\n  - `implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` asserts that a repeated item is recorded once.\n- **Unresolvable inputs reported before inference.**\n  - `unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` runs the CLI with an ignored declaration. It asserts a nonzero exit, that stderr names the path, that the endpoint was never contacted and that the evidence is unchanged.\n  - `fn[unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference]` checks a missing file, a missing node and an ignored anchor.\n  - `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort` in `src/authoring/tools.rs` checks an anchor outside the project.\n  - `fn[unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment]` shows that stale recorded inputs are not mandatory.\n- **Complete set in the initial request.**\n  - The CLI tests assert that the prompt in the first request contains the requirement text, the definition text and the test item. These are `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` and the implementation-discovery test.\n  - `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` asserts that the first prompt contains the item hash, the requirement text and the built-in text.\n  - The site test asserts that `initial.subject` equals the template filled with `model_mandatory_inputs`.\n- **Visibility and denial.**\n  - `fn[disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation]` checks a `.gitignore`d declaration, expecting `PermissionDenied` with the path in the message.\n  - `fn[evidence_anchors_and_aliases_follow_project_ignore_rules]` checks an ignored anchor and an alias path.\n  - `fn[mandatory_inputs_can_read_untracked_declarations_and_terms]` checks that untracked files are available.\n  - The citation test checks that an ignored term file aborts.\n\n**Conclusion**\nEvery testable obligation and the failure and boundary cases it names (denial, ignored files, outside the project, duplicates, the initial request) has a test with concrete assertions. I found no unmarked relevant test and no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "24022a85373a405b0fb3408b99edf1d1bbc96fd33788256d087c885bb430c4d7",
